Profile Management Microservice?
Our Profile Management microservice is responsible for managing customer accounts, authenticating users, and allowing customers to view and update their profile information.

For example, when a customer creates an account on our e-commerce website, they provide information such as:
- First name
- Last name
- Address
- Postal code
- Email address
- Password
The Profile Management microservice stores this information in a MySQL database and provides APIs for registration, login, authentication, and profile updates.

Later, when the customer logs in, the service verifies their credentials and generates a JWT authentication token.

The customer can use this token to access protected endpoints, such as viewing or updating their profile.


| Component  	        | 		Purpose |

| Node.js	        | Executes the JavaScript application |
| Express.js  	        | Creates REST API endpoints |
| MySQL 	        | Stores customer account and profile information |
| `mysql2` 	        | Allows Node.js to communicate with MySQL |
| `jsonwebtoken`        | Generates and verifies JWT authentication tokens |
| `body-parser`         | Parses JSON request bodies |
| `cors` 	        | Configures cross-origin HTTP access |
| `auth_api.js`         | Main application file |
| `package.json`        | Defines application dependencies |
| Docker                | Packages  the application into a container |
| Kubernetes Secret     | Supplies sensitive database credentials to the Pod |
| Kubernetes Deployment | Manages application replicas |
| Kubernetes Service    | Provides a stable network endpoint for the application |
| Port 3003    		| Default HTTP port of the Profile Management API |


|HTTPMethod | Endpoint    | Purpose |

| POST | `/api/signup`    | Registers a new customer |
| POST | `/api/signin`    | Authenticates a customer and generates a JWT |
| POST | `/api/signout`   | Returns a logout response for an authenticated user |
| GET  | `/api/protected` | Retrieves the authenticated user's profile |
| PUT  | `/api/update`    | Updates the authenticated user's profile |
| GET  | `/health/live`   | Checks whether the application is responding |
| GET  | `/health/ready`  | Checks whether the application can communicate with MySQL |


