Docker Containerization: 

Once the application code is correcte we will start setting up the dockerfile:

The Docker image will contain: 
* A node.js runtime
* The auth_api.js application
* package.json
* Installed npm dependnecies

Testing the Docker before the kubernetes:
Create a Docker network:
>> docker network create ecommerce-net

Create a persistent volume:
>> docker network create ecommerce-net

Start the mysql:

docker run -d \
  --name profile-mysql \
  --network ecommerce-net \
  -v profile-mysql-data:/var/lib/mysql \
  -e MYSQL_DATABASE=profile_db \
  -e MYSQL_USER=profile_user \
  -e MYSQL_PASSWORD='<your-test-password>' \
  -e MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD='<your-test-root-password>' \
  mysql:8.4

check the docker mysql logs and  run the Profile managment docker image:

docker run -d \
  --name profile-management \
  --network ecommerce-net \
  -p 3003:3003 \
  -e PORT=3003 \
  -e MYSQL_HOST=profile-mysql \
  -e MYSQL_PORT=3306 \
  -e MYSQL_DATABASE=profile_db \
  -e MYSQL_USER=profile_user \
  -e MYSQL_PASSWORD='<your-test-password>' \
  profile-management:v1


